{"ts": "2026-10-29T09:47:16.215178Z", "run_id": "r-20261029T0947Z-5526", "unit": "openspec:add-api-pep", "seq": 5, "type": "task.started", "task": "6.2", "title": "6.2 Write `src/api/list-filter.test.ts` first (scenarios \"Item filter\", \"Sql filter\", \"Error replies pass unchanged\" and \"Other 2xx payloads refuse\"), then implement `listPredicate(request, firstParam)` in `src/api/list-filter.ts` (returns `listFilter.predicate(request.principal, firstParam)` and marks the request; on a route without a sql filter it throws `RouteDefinitionError` `ROUTE_DEF_INVALID` with `details.reason` `no_sql_filter`) and two hooks that `defineRoute` in `src/api/route.ts` attaches to routes with a `listFilter`, both acting only when `reply.statusCode` is 2xx (any other status, an error envelope, passes unchanged). The `preSerialization` hook: `item` requires an object payload with an `items` array (else a thrown `Error`, 500 `INTERNAL`) and keeps the items for which `await canRead(request.principal, item)` is true, other members unchanged; `sql` throws an `Error` logged `LIST_FILTER_NOT_APPLIED` when the request was not marked; it then marks the request as filtered. The `onSend` hook throws an `Error` (500 `INTERNAL`, nothing sent) for a 2xx reply whose request was not marked as filtered, which is what a string, Buffer, stream or null payload is, since Fastify skips `preSerialization` for them, implementing requirement \"A list route never returns items the principal cannot read\""}
